        ":question/id": "8bbb774c-4bbb-58f8-84cb-fd20b0029b02",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-73638",
        ":question/problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & ↔{R}_{4} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $4$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns."
      }
